6. Old-symbol and collision audit

A whitespace-tolerant search using
`\\omega\s*(?:\{\s*\})?\s*_\s*(?:\{\s*0\s*\}|0)`, together with searches
for `\omega_0`, `omega_0`, `omega 0`, `omega0`, `ω₀`, `ω_0`, and `ω 0`,
returns no occurrence in the corrected canonical source or extracted PDF text.
No intentional old occurrence remains. The earlier literal 15b search did not
establish this because it missed `\omega _0`; that defect is now corrected.

Existing uppercase-delta uses were inspected. `\Delta_{\rm WI}` is the
coefficient-growth characteristic; `\Delta_j` denotes level differences;
`\Delta S` denotes an action difference; and `\Delta_{k,n}^{(j)}` denotes
indexed perturbative contributions. All are explicitly subscripted or followed
by `S`, locally defined, and visually distinct from the bare model detuning
`\Delta`; no ambiguous collision was found. The former `\Delta_E` and
`\Delta_\omega` convention paragraph was removed in favor of the prompt's
concise opposite-convention statement.

